('113.49.c.9.E',3,'Paying bills 30 days late repeatedly will most likely do what?','["Improve rates", "Raise it", "Lower your credit score", "Remove debt"]'::jsonb,2,'Payment history is a key factor.','original'),
('113.49.c.9.E',3,'A consequence of poor credit management can be what?','["Instant approvals", "Lower interest rates", "Free credit", "Higher interest rates and difficulty renting or getting loans"]'::jsonb,3,'Poor credit raises costs.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.A',3,'APR stands for what?','["Annual percentage rate", "Applied profit ratio", "Average price range", "Annual payment return"]'::jsonb,0,'APR expresses yearly borrowing cost.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.A',3,'A fixed interest rate on a loan does what?','["Changes monthly", "Stays the same for the life of the loan", "Disappears", "Rises with the market"]'::jsonb,1,'A variable rate can change.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.B',3,'A larger down payment reduces the total cost of borrowing because what?','["Interest is higher", "Fees double", "Less money is borrowed, so less interest accrues", "The loan term is longer"]'::jsonb,2,'Principal is smaller.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.B',3,'Making extra payments toward principal helps by doing what?','["Adding fees", "Extending the term", "Increasing interest", "Reducing interest costs and paying off the loan sooner"]'::jsonb,3,'Extra principal payments save money.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.C',3,'A debit card differs from a credit card in that a debit card does what?','["Withdraws money directly from your bank account", "Builds credit by itself", "Borrows from the bank", "Charges interest monthly"]'::jsonb,0,'Debit uses your own funds.','original'),
('113.49.c.10.C',3,'Carrying a balance on a credit card leads to what?','["Lower balance automatically", "Interest charges added to what you owe", "No cost", "Free money"]'::jsonb,1,'Paying in full avoids interest.','original'),
('113.49.c.11.A',3,'Financial risk can be defined as what?','["A guaranteed gain", "A tax benefit", "The possible loss of assets or earning potential", "An interest rate"]'::jsonb,2,'Risk involves chance of loss.','original'),
('113.49.c.11.A',3,'Which event is a financial risk?','["Winning a prize", "Earning interest", "Getting a raise", "Losing a job"]'::jsonb,3,'Job loss reduces earning potential.','original'),
('113.49.c.11.B',3,'Buying insurance to protect against a major loss is an example of which risk strategy?','["Transferring risk", "Retaining risk", "Avoiding risk", "Ignoring risk"]'::jsonb,0,'The insurer takes on the risk.','original'),
('113.49.c.11.B',3,'Choosing not to take a dangerous activity is what risk strategy?','["Transferring risk", "Avoiding risk", "Reducing risk", "Retaining risk"]'::jsonb,1,'Avoidance eliminates exposure.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.A',3,'Dana pays $120 every month to keep her auto policy active. What is that payment called?','["A policy limit", "A deductible", "A premium", "A co-pay"]'::jsonb,2,'A deductible is the amount you pay before coverage.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.A',3,'A policy has a $500 deductible and a $10,000 policy limit. What does the $10,000 represent?','["The amount paid before coverage starts", "The monthly payment", "A fixed fee per visit", "The maximum amount the insurer will pay for a covered loss"]'::jsonb,3,'Higher deductibles often mean lower premiums.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.B',3,'Employer-sponsored health insurance often costs less than individual coverage because what?','["Employers usually share part of the premium", "There are no premiums", "Coverage is free", "Deductibles are zero"]'::jsonb,0,'Employers subsidize group plans.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.C',3,'Disability insurance protects against what?','["Home theft", "Loss of income if you cannot work due to illness or injury", "Tax bills", "Car repairs"]'::jsonb,1,'It replaces part of earnings.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.D',3,'Term life insurance differs from whole life insurance in that term insurance does what?','["Never expires", "Builds cash value", "Covers a set period and usually costs less", "Costs more"]'::jsonb,2,'Whole life builds cash value.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.D',3,'Life insurance is most important for people who do what?','["Are retired with no obligations", "Have no dependents", "Own no property", "Have dependents who rely on their income"]'::jsonb,3,'It protects survivors.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.E',3,'Renter''s insurance generally covers what?','["The renter''s belongings and liability", "The landlord''s income", "The building structure", "Rent payments"]'::jsonb,0,'The landlord insures the building.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.E',3,'Homeowner''s insurance generally covers what?','["Mortgage interest", "Damage to the home and personal property from covered events", "Utilities", "Property taxes"]'::jsonb,1,'Policies list covered perils.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.F',3,'Which factor can raise the price of automobile insurance?','["Few miles driven", "A clean record", "A history of accidents or tickets", "Safe driving courses"]'::jsonb,2,'Risk drives prices.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.G',3,'An extended warranty is best described as what?','["A required item", "A free service", "A tax", "Optional coverage that may not be worth its cost"]'::jsonb,3,'Compare the cost with likely repairs.','original'),
('113.49.c.12.G',3,'Mortgage insurance is usually required when a buyer does what?','["Makes a small down payment", "Buys a condo only", "Rents", "Pays in cash"]'::jsonb,0,'It protects the lender.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.A',3,'Which action helps prevent identity theft?','["Posting your Social Security number", "Shredding documents with personal information", "Sharing your PIN", "Using one password everywhere"]'::jsonb,1,'Protect personal data.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.A',3,'A strong password is one that does what?','["Is the same everywhere", "Is your birthday", "Is long, unique and hard to guess", "Is short"]'::jsonb,2,'Use unique passwords.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.B',3,'An email that urges you to click a link and confirm your bank password is most likely what?','["A bank statement", "A free gift", "A tax refund", "A phishing scam"]'::jsonb,3,'Phishing tricks people into giving information.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.B',3,'A pyramid scheme earns money mainly by doing what?','["Recruiting new participants who pay in", "Paying taxes", "Selling real products", "Investing in stocks"]'::jsonb,0,'It collapses when recruitment stops.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.C',3,'The Better Business Bureau helps consumers by doing what?','["Setting interest rates", "Providing business ratings and handling complaints", "Collecting taxes", "Printing money"]'::jsonb,1,'Consumer protection agencies help resolve disputes.','original'),
('113.49.c.13.C',3,'Which agency regulates consumer financial products like credit cards and mortgages?','["The Post Office", "The NFL", "The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau", "The Weather Service"]'::jsonb,2,'The CFPB protects consumers.','original'),
('113.49.c.14.A',3,'A will is a legal document that does what?','["Appoints a doctor", "Sets taxes", "Pays bills", "Directs how your property is distributed after death"]'::jsonb,3,'Wills also name guardians for minor children.','original'),
('113.49.c.14.A',3,'A beneficiary designation on a retirement account does what?','["Names who receives the account after the owner dies", "Sets the interest", "Names the bank", "Lists the fees"]'::jsonb,0,'Designations usually override wills.','original'),
('113.49.c.14.B',3,'A power of attorney allows someone to do what?','["Receive your paycheck", "Act on your behalf in legal or financial matters", "Write your will", "Vote for you"]'::jsonb,1,'You choose a trusted agent.','original'),
('113.49.c.14.B',3,'A living will states what?','["Where your property goes", "Your tax return", "Your wishes for medical treatment if you cannot speak for yourself", "Your funeral costs"]'::jsonb,2,'It guides end-of-life care.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
